From 922a69936017f68696905800aaa090758449f2c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 092/172] drm/display: bridge_connector: restore the max bpc
 default

drm_bridge_connector_create_state() leaves max_requested_bpc at 0, a
value userspace cannot set because the max bpc property range starts at
8. Downstream bridges then refuse every deep color format.

Initialise max_requested_bpc to the maximum of the max bpc property,
which is the default drm_connector_attach_max_bpc_property() applies.

Signed-off-by: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_bridge_connector.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_bridge_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_bridge_connector.c
index 8b54069fa53a..6ab10b00756c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_bridge_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_bridge_connector.c
@@ -276,6 +276,10 @@ drm_bridge_connector_create_state(struct drm_connector *connector)
 	if (IS_ERR(conn_state))
 		return conn_state;
 
+	if (connector->max_bpc_property)
+		conn_state->max_requested_bpc =
+			connector->max_bpc_property->values[1];
+
 	if (bridge_connector->bridge_hdmi)
 		__drm_atomic_helper_connector_hdmi_state_init(connector,
 							      conn_state);
-- 
